---@field jobCreationReason? gcp.bigquery_v2.JobCreationReason Optional. The reason why a Job was created. Only relevant when a job_reference is present in the response. If job_reference is not present it will always be unset.
---@field totalBytesProcessed? string The total number of bytes processed for this query. If this query was a dry run, this is the number of bytes that would be processed if the query were run.
---@field cacheHit? boolean Whether the query result was fetched from the query cache.
---@field numDmlAffectedRows? string Output only. The number of rows affected by a DML statement. Present only for DML statements INSERT, UPDATE or DELETE.
---@field totalSlotMs? string Output only. Number of slot ms the user is actually billed for.
---@field totalBytesBilled? string Output only. If the project is configured to use on-demand pricing, then this field contains the total bytes billed for the job. If the project is configured to use flat-rate pricing, then you are not billed for bytes and this field is informational only.
---@field queryId? string Auto-generated ID for the query.
---@field totalRows? string The total number of rows in the complete query result set, which can be more than the number of rows in this single page of results.

---Summary of the state of query execution at a given time.
---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.QueryTimelineSample
---@field elapsedMs? string Milliseconds elapsed since the start of query execution.
---@field estimatedRunnableUnits? string Units of work that can be scheduled immediately. Providing additional slots for these units of work will accelerate the query, if no other query in the reservation needs additional slots.
---@field activeUnits? string Total number of active workers. This does not correspond directly to slot usage. This is the largest value observed since the last sample.
---@field completedUnits? string Total parallel units of work completed by this query.
---@field shuffleRamUsageRatio? number Total shuffle usage ratio in shuffle RAM per reservation of this query. This will be provided for reservation customers only.
---@field totalSlotMs? string Cumulative slot-ms consumed by the query.
---@field pendingUnits? string Total units of work remaining for the query. This number can be revised (increased or decreased) while the query is running.

---@alias gcp.bigquery_v2.QueryTimelineSampleList gcp.bigquery_v2.QueryTimelineSample[]

---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.RangePartitioning
---@field field? string Required. The name of the column to partition the table on. It must be a top-level, INT64 column whose mode is NULLABLE or REQUIRED.
---@field range? gcp.bigquery_v2.RangePartitioningRange [Experimental] Defines the ranges for range partitioning.

---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.RangePartitioningRange
---@field start? string [Experimental] The start of range partitioning, inclusive.
---@field interval? string [Experimental] The width of each interval.
---@field ["end"]? string [Experimental] The end of range partitioning, exclusive.

---Represents the value of a range.
---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.RangeValue
---@field start? gcp.bigquery_v2.QueryParameterValue Optional. The start value of the range. A missing value represents an unbounded start.
---@field ["end"]? gcp.bigquery_v2.QueryParameterValue Optional. The end value of the range. A missing value represents an unbounded end.

---Evaluation metrics used by weighted-ALS models specified by feedback_type=implicit.
---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.RankingMetrics
---@field meanSquaredError? number Similar to the mean squared error computed in regression and explicit recommendation models except instead of computing the rating directly, the output from evaluate is computed against a preference which is 1 or 0 depending on if the rating exists or not.
---@field meanAveragePrecision? number Calculates a precision per user for all the items by ranking them and then averages all the precisions across all the users.
---@field normalizedDiscountedCumulativeGain? number A metric to determine the goodness of a ranking calculated from the predicted confidence by comparing it to an ideal rank measured by the original ratings.
---@field averageRank? number Determines the goodness of a ranking by computing the percentile rank from the predicted confidence and dividing it by the original rank.

---Evaluation metrics for regression and explicit feedback type matrix factorization models.
---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.RegressionMetrics
---@field meanSquaredLogError? number Mean squared log error.
---@field rSquared? number R^2 score. This corresponds to r2_score in ML.EVALUATE.
---@field meanAbsoluteError? number Mean absolute error.
---@field meanSquaredError? number Mean squared error.
---@field medianAbsoluteError? number Median absolute error.

---Options for a remote user-defined function.
---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.RemoteFunctionOptions
---@field userDefinedContext? gcp.bigquery_v2.StringMap User-defined context as a set of key/value pairs, which will be sent as function invocation context together with batched arguments in the requests to the remote service. The total number of bytes of keys and values must be less than 8KB.
---@field endpoint? string Endpoint of the user-provided remote service, e.g. ```https://us-east1-my_gcf_project.cloudfunctions.net/remote_add```
---@field maxBatchingRows? string Max number of rows in each batch sent to the remote service. If absent or if 0, BigQuery dynamically decides the number of rows in a batch.
---@field connection? string Fully qualified name of the user-provided connection object which holds the authentication information to send requests to the remote service. Format: ```"projects/{projectId}/locations/{locationId}/connections/{connectionId}"```

---Remote Model Info
---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.RemoteModelInfo
---@field maxBatchingRows? string Output only. Max number of rows in each batch sent to the remote service. If unset, the number of rows in each batch is set dynamically.
---@field connection? string Output only. Fully qualified name of the user-provided connection object of the remote model. Format: ```"projects/{project_id}/locations/{location_id}/connections/{connection_id}"```
---@field speechRecognizer? string Output only. The name of the speech recognizer to use for speech recognition. The expected format is `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/recognizers/{recognizer}`. Customers can specify this field at model creation. If not specified, a default recognizer `projects/{model project}/locations/global/recognizers/_` will be used. See more details at [recognizers](https://cloud.google.com/speech-to-text/v2/docs/reference/rest/v2/projects.locations.recognizers)
---@field remoteServiceType? gcp.bigquery_v2.RemoteModelInfoRemoteServiceTypeEnum|string Output only. The remote service type for remote model.
---@field remoteModelVersion? string Output only. The model version for LLM.
---@field endpoint? string Output only. The endpoint for remote model.

---@alias gcp.bigquery_v2.RemoteModelInfoRemoteServiceTypeEnum "REMOTE_SERVICE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"CLOUD_AI_TRANSLATE_V3"|"CLOUD_AI_VISION_V1"|"CLOUD_AI_NATURAL_LANGUAGE_V1"|"CLOUD_AI_SPEECH_TO_TEXT_V2"

---The replica metadata of the dataset. If the dataset has two or more replicas, it's considered a cross region replicated (CRR) dataset.
---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.Replica
---@field failoverReservationUri? string Output only. Failover reservation ID for the replica's region if this replica is used for DR. Fully-qualified format, e.g. "projects/some-project/locations/US/reservations/some-reservation" The location portion of the format is upper case if "US" or "EU", otherwise a lower case cloud region like "asia-northeast1".
---@field creationTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the replica was created. For any dataset's first replica, this should be set to the dataset's creation_time.
---@field replicaOptions? gcp.bigquery_v2.ReplicaOptions Optional. Contains modify options on the replica such as set a kms key on the replica.
---@field location? string Required. The logical bigquery region where this replica is located. This is upper case if "US" or "EU", otherwise a lower case cloud region like "asia-northeast1".
---@field primaryAssignmentTime? string Output only. The time at which the replica was assigned primary. Only one replica will have this field populated at any point.
---@field id? string Required. The user-visible string identifier for this dataset replica. This is generally named after the region.
---@field backfillCompletionTime? string Output only. The time when the backfill was completed and replica is ready to use.
---@field primaryAssignmentCompletionTime? string Output only. After a new primary assignment is made, this is the time that the dataset's data has been fully replicated to the replica, and after which the system will use current reads in the new primary replica.
---@field replicaState? gcp.bigquery_v2.ReplicaReplicaStateEnum|string Output only. Gives an explicit indicator of the replica primary state.

---@alias gcp.bigquery_v2.ReplicaList gcp.bigquery_v2.Replica[]

---Options set by the user when creating the replica. These include region-specific dataset values, for example default KMS key name. When a resource is replicated, the destination region's replica contains values that should be overwritten in the destination region.
---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.ReplicaOptions
---@field defaultKmsKeyName? string Optional. Default KMS encryption key name.

---@alias gcp.bigquery_v2.ReplicaReplicaStateEnum "REPLICA_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PRIMARY"|"SECONDARY"|"ASSIGNED_PRIMARY"|"PREVIOUSLY_ASSIGNED_PRIMARY"|"BACKFILLING"

---Output-only policy member strings of a Google Cloud resource's built-in identity.
---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.ResourcePolicyMember
---@field iamPolicyUidPrincipal? string Output only. IAM policy binding member referring to a Google Cloud resource by system-assigned unique identifier (https://google.aip.dev/148#uid). If a resource is deleted and recreated with the same name, the binding will not be applicable to the new resource Example: `principal://parametermanager.googleapis.com/projects/12345/uid/locations/us-central1-a/parameters/a918fed5`
---@field iamPolicyNamePrincipal? string Output only. IAM policy binding member referring to a Google Cloud resource by user-assigned name (https://google.aip.dev/122). If a resource is deleted and recreated with the same name, the binding will be applicable to the new resource. Example: `principal://parametermanager.googleapis.com/projects/12345/name/locations/us-central1-a/parameters/my-parameter`

---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.RestrictionConfig
---@field type? gcp.bigquery_v2.RestrictionConfigTypeEnum|string Output only. Specifies the type of dataset/table restriction.

---@alias gcp.bigquery_v2.RestrictionConfigTypeEnum "RESTRICTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"RESTRICTED_DATA_EGRESS"

---A user-defined function or a stored procedure.
---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.Routine
---@field returnTableType? gcp.bigquery_v2.StandardSqlTableType Optional. Can be set only if routine_type = "TABLE_VALUED_FUNCTION". If absent, the return table type is inferred from definition_body at query time in each query that references this routine. If present, then the columns in the evaluated table result will be cast to match the column types specified in return table type, at query time.
---@field creationTime? string Output only. The time when this routine was created, in milliseconds since the epoch.
---@field lastModifiedTime? string Output only. The time when this routine was last modified, in milliseconds since the epoch.
---@field description? string Optional. The description of the routine, if defined.
---@field routineType? gcp.bigquery_v2.RoutineRoutineTypeEnum Required. The type of routine.
---@field determinismLevel? gcp.bigquery_v2.RoutineDeterminismLevelEnum Optional. The determinism level of the JavaScript UDF, if defined.
---@field language? gcp.bigquery_v2.RoutineLanguageEnum Optional. Defaults to "SQL" if remote_function_options field is absent, not set otherwise.
---@field pythonOptions? gcp.bigquery_v2.PythonOptions Optional. Options for the Python UDF. [Preview](https://cloud.google.com/products/#product-launch-stages)
---@field buildStatus? gcp.bigquery_v2.RoutineBuildStatus Output only. The build status of the routine. This field is only applicable to Python UDFs. [Preview](https://cloud.google.com/products/#product-launch-stages)
---@field arguments? gcp.bigquery_v2.ArgumentList Optional.
---@field dataGovernanceType? gcp.bigquery_v2.RoutineDataGovernanceTypeEnum Optional. If set to `DATA_MASKING`, the function is validated and made available as a masking function. For more information, see [Create custom masking routines](https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/user-defined-functions#custom-mask).
---@field etag? string Output only. A hash of this resource.
---@field importedLibraries? gcp.bigquery_v2.StringList Optional. If language = "JAVASCRIPT", this field stores the path of the imported JAVASCRIPT libraries.
---@field definitionBody? string Required. The body of the routine. For functions, this is the expression in the AS clause. If `language = "SQL"`, it is the substring inside (but excluding) the parentheses. For example, for the function created with the following statement: `CREATE FUNCTION JoinLines(x string, y string) as (concat(x, "\n", y))` The definition_body is `concat(x, "\n", y)` (\n is not replaced with linebreak). If `language="JAVASCRIPT"`, it is the evaluated string in the AS clause. For example, for the function created with the following statement: `CREATE FUNCTION f() RETURNS STRING LANGUAGE js AS 'return "\n";\n'` The definition_body is `return "\n";\n` Note that both \n are replaced with linebreaks. If `definition_body` references another routine, then that routine must be fully qualified with its project ID.
---@field strictMode? boolean Optional. Use this option to catch many common errors. Error checking is not exhaustive, and successfully creating a procedure doesn't guarantee that the procedure will successfully execute at runtime. If `strictMode` is set to `TRUE`, the procedure body is further checked for errors such as non-existent tables or columns. The `CREATE PROCEDURE` statement fails if the body fails any of these checks. If `strictMode` is set to `FALSE`, the procedure body is checked only for syntax. For procedures that invoke themselves recursively, specify `strictMode=FALSE` to avoid non-existent procedure errors during validation. Default value is `TRUE`.
---@field externalRuntimeOptions? gcp.bigquery_v2.ExternalRuntimeOptions Optional. Options for the runtime of the external system executing the routine. This field is only applicable for Python UDFs. [Preview](https://cloud.google.com/products/#product-launch-stages)
---@field sparkOptions? gcp.bigquery_v2.SparkOptions Optional. Spark specific options.
---@field routineReference? gcp.bigquery_v2.RoutineReference Required. Reference describing the ID of this routine.
---@field remoteFunctionOptions? gcp.bigquery_v2.RemoteFunctionOptions Optional. Remote function specific options.
---@field returnType? gcp.bigquery_v2.StandardSqlDataType Optional if language = "SQL"; required otherwise. Cannot be set if routine_type = "TABLE_VALUED_FUNCTION". If absent, the return type is inferred from definition_body at query time in each query that references this routine. If present, then the evaluated result will be cast to the specified returned type at query time. For example, for the functions created with the following statements: * `CREATE FUNCTION Add(x FLOAT64, y FLOAT64) RETURNS FLOAT64 AS (x + y);` * `CREATE FUNCTION Increment(x FLOAT64) AS (Add(x, 1));` * `CREATE FUNCTION Decrement(x FLOAT64) RETURNS FLOAT64 AS (Add(x, -1));` The return_type is `{type_kind: "FLOAT64"}` for `Add` and `Decrement`, and is absent for `Increment` (inferred as FLOAT64 at query time). Suppose the function `Add` is replaced by `CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION Add(x INT64, y INT64) AS (x + y);` Then the inferred return type of `Increment` is automatically changed to INT64 at query time, while the return type of `Decrement` remains FLOAT64.
---@field securityMode? gcp.bigquery_v2.RoutineSecurityModeEnum Optional. The security mode of the routine, if defined. If not defined, the security mode is automatically determined from the routine's configuration.

---The status of a routine build.
---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.RoutineBuildStatus
---@field installedPackages? gcp.bigquery_v2.InstalledPackageList Output only. The list of installed packages in the routine's execution environment. Populated only after the build succeeds.
---@field buildDuration? string Output only. The time taken for the image build. Populated only after the build succeeds or fails.
---@field buildState? gcp.bigquery_v2.RoutineBuildStatusBuildStateEnum|string Output only. The current build state of the routine.
---@field errorResult? gcp.bigquery_v2.ErrorProto Output only. A result object that will be present only if the build has failed.
---@field imageSizeBytes? string Output only. The size of the image in bytes. Populated only after the build succeeds.
---@field buildStateUpdateTime? string Output only. The time when the build state was updated last.

---@alias gcp.bigquery_v2.RoutineBuildStatusBuildStateEnum "BUILD_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"IN_PROGRESS"|"SUCCEEDED"|"FAILED"

---@alias gcp.bigquery_v2.RoutineDataGovernanceTypeEnum "DATA_GOVERNANCE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"DATA_MASKING"

---@alias gcp.bigquery_v2.RoutineDeterminismLevelEnum "DETERMINISM_LEVEL_UNSPECIFIED"|"DETERMINISTIC"|"NOT_DETERMINISTIC"

---@alias gcp.bigquery_v2.RoutineLanguageEnum "LANGUAGE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SQL"|"JAVASCRIPT"|"PYTHON"|"JAVA"|"SCALA"

