---Options for a user-defined Spark routine.
---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.SparkOptions
---@field jarUris? gcp.bigquery_v2.StringList JARs to include on the driver and executor CLASSPATH. For more information about Apache Spark, see [Apache Spark](https://spark.apache.org/docs/latest/index.html).
---@field properties? gcp.bigquery_v2.StringMap Configuration properties as a set of key/value pairs, which will be passed on to the Spark application. For more information, see [Apache Spark](https://spark.apache.org/docs/latest/index.html) and the [procedure option list](https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/data-definition-language#procedure_option_list).
---@field pyFileUris? gcp.bigquery_v2.StringList Python files to be placed on the PYTHONPATH for PySpark application. Supported file types: `.py`, `.egg`, and `.zip`. For more information about Apache Spark, see [Apache Spark](https://spark.apache.org/docs/latest/index.html).
---@field mainClass? string The fully qualified name of a class in jar_uris, for example, com.example.wordcount. Exactly one of main_class and main_jar_uri field should be set for Java/Scala language type.
---@field archiveUris? gcp.bigquery_v2.StringList Archive files to be extracted into the working directory of each executor. For more information about Apache Spark, see [Apache Spark](https://spark.apache.org/docs/latest/index.html).
---@field containerImage? string Custom container image for the runtime environment.
---@field fileUris? gcp.bigquery_v2.StringList Files to be placed in the working directory of each executor. For more information about Apache Spark, see [Apache Spark](https://spark.apache.org/docs/latest/index.html).
---@field connection? string Fully qualified name of the user-provided Spark connection object. Format: ```"projects/{project_id}/locations/{location_id}/connections/{connection_id}"```
---@field runtimeVersion? string Runtime version. If not specified, the default runtime version is used.
---@field mainFileUri? string The main file/jar URI of the Spark application. Exactly one of the definition_body field and the main_file_uri field must be set for Python. Exactly one of main_class and main_file_uri field should be set for Java/Scala language type.

---Statistics for a BigSpark query. Populated as part of JobStatistics2
---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.SparkStatistics
---@field loggingInfo? gcp.bigquery_v2.SparkLoggingInfo Output only. Logging info is used to generate a link to Cloud Logging.
---@field kmsKeyName? string Output only. The Cloud KMS encryption key that is used to protect the resources created by the Spark job. If the Spark procedure uses the invoker security mode, the Cloud KMS encryption key is either inferred from the provided system variable, `@@spark_proc_properties.kms_key_name`, or the default key of the BigQuery job's project (if the CMEK organization policy is enforced). Otherwise, the Cloud KMS key is either inferred from the Spark connection associated with the procedure (if it is provided), or from the default key of the Spark connection's project if the CMEK organization policy is enforced. Example: * `projects/[kms_project_id]/locations/[region]/keyRings/[key_region]/cryptoKeys/[key]`
---@field sparkJobId? string Output only. Spark job ID if a Spark job is created successfully.
---@field gcsStagingBucket? string Output only. The Google Cloud Storage bucket that is used as the default file system by the Spark application. This field is only filled when the Spark procedure uses the invoker security mode. The `gcsStagingBucket` bucket is inferred from the `@@spark_proc_properties.staging_bucket` system variable (if it is provided). Otherwise, BigQuery creates a default staging bucket for the job and returns the bucket name in this field. Example: * `gs://[bucket_name]`
---@field sparkJobLocation? string Output only. Location where the Spark job is executed. A location is selected by BigQueury for jobs configured to run in a multi-region.
---@field endpoints? gcp.bigquery_v2.StringMap Output only. Endpoints returned from Dataproc. Key list: - history_server_endpoint: A link to Spark job UI.

