---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.TimePartitioning
---@field field? string Optional. If not set, the table is partitioned by pseudo column '_PARTITIONTIME'; if set, the table is partitioned by this field. The field must be a top-level TIMESTAMP or DATE field. Its mode must be NULLABLE or REQUIRED. A wrapper is used here because an empty string is an invalid value.
---@field requirePartitionFilter? boolean If set to true, queries over this table require a partition filter that can be used for partition elimination to be specified. This field is deprecated; please set the field with the same name on the table itself instead. This field needs a wrapper because we want to output the default value, false, if the user explicitly set it.
---@field type? string Required. The supported types are DAY, HOUR, MONTH, and YEAR, which will generate one partition per day, hour, month, and year, respectively.
---@field expirationMs? string Optional. Number of milliseconds for which to keep the storage for a partition. A wrapper is used here because 0 is an invalid value.

---Options used in model training.
---@class gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptions
---@field numTrials? string Number of trials to run this hyperparameter tuning job.
---@field feedbackType? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsFeedbackTypeEnum|string Feedback type that specifies which algorithm to run for matrix factorization.
---@field l2Regularization? number L2 regularization coefficient.
---@field scaleFeatures? boolean If true, scale the feature values by dividing the feature standard deviation. Currently only apply to PCA.
---@field timeSeriesTimestampColumn? string Column to be designated as time series timestamp for ARIMA model.
---@field maxReplicaCount? string The maximum number of machine replicas that will be deployed on an endpoint. The default value is equal to min_replica_count.
---@field autoClassWeights? boolean Whether to calculate class weights automatically based on the popularity of each label.
---@field endpointIdleTtl? string The idle TTL of the endpoint before the resources get destroyed. The default value is 6.5 hours.
---@field colorSpace? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsColorSpaceEnum|string Enums for color space, used for processing images in Object Table. See more details at https://www.tensorflow.org/io/tutorials/colorspace.
---@field standardizeFeatures? boolean Whether to standardize numerical features. Default to true.
---@field forecastLimitLowerBound? number The forecast limit lower bound that was used during ARIMA model training with limits. To see more details of the algorithm: https://otexts.com/fpp2/limits.html
---@field dataSplitMethod? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsDataSplitMethodEnum|string The data split type for training and evaluation, e.g. RANDOM.
---@field maxTreeDepth? string Maximum depth of a tree for boosted tree models.
---@field dropout? number Dropout probability for dnn models.
---@field dartNormalizeType? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsDartNormalizeTypeEnum|string Type of normalization algorithm for boosted tree models using dart booster.
---@field activationFn? string Activation function of the neural nets.
---@field enableGlobalExplain? boolean If true, enable global explanation during training.
---@field timeSeriesLengthFraction? number The fraction of the interpolated length of the time series that's used to model the time series trend component. All of the time points of the time series are used to model the non-trend component. This training option accelerates modeling training without sacrificing much forecasting accuracy. You can use this option with `minTimeSeriesLength` but not with `maxTimeSeriesLength`.
---@field minSplitLoss? number Minimum split loss for boosted tree models.
---@field isTestColumn? string Name of the column used to determine the rows corresponding to control and test. Applies to contribution analysis models.
---@field l1Regularization? number L1 regularization coefficient.
---@field reservationAffinityKey? string Corresponds to the label key of a reservation resource used by Vertex AI. To target a SPECIFIC_RESERVATION by name, use `compute.googleapis.com/reservation-name` as the key and specify the name of your reservation as its value.
---@field colsampleBytree? number Subsample ratio of columns when constructing each tree for boosted tree models.
---@field minReplicaCount? string The minimum number of machine replicas that will be always deployed on an endpoint. This value must be greater than or equal to 1. The default value is 1.
---@field autoArimaMinOrder? string The min value of the sum of non-seasonal p and q.
---@field horizon? string The number of periods ahead that need to be forecasted.
---@field optimizer? string Optimizer used for training the neural nets.
---@field integratedGradientsNumSteps? string Number of integral steps for the integrated gradients explain method.
---@field autoArimaMaxOrder? string The max value of the sum of non-seasonal p and q.
---@field dataFrequency? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsDataFrequencyEnum|string The data frequency of a time series.
---@field pcaExplainedVarianceRatio? number The minimum ratio of cumulative explained variance that needs to be given by the PCA model.
---@field dimensionIdColumns? gcp.bigquery_v2.StringList Optional. Names of the columns to slice on. Applies to contribution analysis models.
---@field holidayRegion? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsHolidayRegionEnum|string The geographical region based on which the holidays are considered in time series modeling. If a valid value is specified, then holiday effects modeling is enabled.
---@field lossType? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsLossTypeEnum|string Type of loss function used during training run.
---@field inputLabelColumns? gcp.bigquery_v2.StringList Name of input label columns in training data.
---@field xgboostVersion? string User-selected XGBoost versions for training of XGBoost models.
---@field sampledShapleyNumPaths? string Number of paths for the sampled Shapley explain method.
---@field colsampleBylevel? number Subsample ratio of columns for each level for boosted tree models.
---@field modelRegistry? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsModelRegistryEnum|string The model registry.
---@field warmStart? boolean Whether to train a model from the last checkpoint.
---@field minRelativeProgress? number When early_stop is true, stops training when accuracy improvement is less than 'min_relative_progress'. Used only for iterative training algorithms.
---@field kmeansInitializationColumn? string The column used to provide the initial centroids for kmeans algorithm when kmeans_initialization_method is CUSTOM.
---@field minTreeChildWeight? string Minimum sum of instance weight needed in a child for boosted tree models.
---@field cleanSpikesAndDips? boolean If true, clean spikes and dips in the input time series.
---@field adjustStepChanges? boolean If true, detect step changes and make data adjustment in the input time series.
---@field learnRateStrategy? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsLearnRateStrategyEnum|string The strategy to determine learn rate for the current iteration.
---@field maxParallelTrials? string Maximum number of trials to run in parallel.
---@field modelGardenModelName? string The name of a Vertex model garden publisher model. Format is `publishers/{publisher}/models/{model}@{optional_version_id}`.
---@field minTimeSeriesLength? string The minimum number of time points in a time series that are used in modeling the trend component of the time series. If you use this option you must also set the `timeSeriesLengthFraction` option. This training option ensures that enough time points are available when you use `timeSeriesLengthFraction` in trend modeling. This is particularly important when forecasting multiple time series in a single query using `timeSeriesIdColumn`. If the total number of time points is less than the `minTimeSeriesLength` value, then the query uses all available time points.
---@field numPrincipalComponents? string Number of principal components to keep in the PCA model. Must be <= the number of features.
---@field hiddenUnits? gcp.bigquery_v2.StringList Hidden units for dnn models.
---@field maxIterations? string The maximum number of iterations in training. Used only for iterative training algorithms.
---@field machineType? string The type of the machine used to deploy and serve the model.
---@field holidayRegions? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsHolidayRegionsItemEnumList A list of geographical regions that are used for time series modeling.
---@field instanceWeightColumn? string Name of the instance weight column for training data. This column isn't be used as a feature.
---@field batchSize? string Batch size for dnn models.
---@field huggingFaceModelId? string The id of a Hugging Face model. For example, `google/gemma-2-2b-it`.
---@field colsampleBynode? number Subsample ratio of columns for each node(split) for boosted tree models.
---@field earlyStop? boolean Whether to stop early when the loss doesn't improve significantly any more (compared to min_relative_progress). Used only for iterative training algorithms.
---@field learnRate? number Learning rate in training. Used only for iterative training algorithms.
---@field budgetHours? number Budget in hours for AutoML training.
---@field nonSeasonalOrder? gcp.bigquery_v2.ArimaOrder A specification of the non-seasonal part of the ARIMA model: the three components (p, d, q) are the AR order, the degree of differencing, and the MA order.
---@field autoArima? boolean Whether to enable auto ARIMA or not.
---@field numParallelTree? string Number of parallel trees constructed during each iteration for boosted tree models.
---@field boosterType? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsBoosterTypeEnum|string Booster type for boosted tree models.
---@field userColumn? string User column specified for matrix factorization models.
---@field vertexAiModelVersionAliases? gcp.bigquery_v2.StringList The version aliases to apply in Vertex AI model registry. Always overwrite if the version aliases exists in a existing model.
---@field numClusters? string Number of clusters for clustering models.
---@field itemColumn? string Item column specified for matrix factorization models.
---@field kmeansInitializationMethod? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsKmeansInitializationMethodEnum|string The method used to initialize the centroids for kmeans algorithm.
---@field pcaSolver? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsPcaSolverEnum|string The solver for PCA.
---@field decomposeTimeSeries? boolean If true, perform decompose time series and save the results.
---@field initialLearnRate? number Specifies the initial learning rate for the line search learn rate strategy.
---@field dataSplitColumn? string The column to split data with. This column won't be used as a feature. 1. When data_split_method is CUSTOM, the corresponding column should be boolean. The rows with true value tag are eval data, and the false are training data. 2. When data_split_method is SEQ, the first DATA_SPLIT_EVAL_FRACTION rows (from smallest to largest) in the corresponding column are used as training data, and the rest are eval data. It respects the order in Orderable data types: https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/data-types#data_type_properties
---@field maxTimeSeriesLength? string The maximum number of time points in a time series that can be used in modeling the trend component of the time series. Don't use this option with the `timeSeriesLengthFraction` or `minTimeSeriesLength` options.
---@field modelUri? string Google Cloud Storage URI from which the model was imported. Only applicable for imported models.
---@field reservationAffinityType? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsReservationAffinityTypeEnum|string Specifies the reservation affinity type used to configure a Vertex AI resource. The default value is `NO_RESERVATION`.
---@field optimizationStrategy? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsOptimizationStrategyEnum|string Optimization strategy for training linear regression models.
---@field minAprioriSupport? number The apriori support minimum. Applies to contribution analysis models.
---@field walsAlpha? number Hyperparameter for matrix factoration when implicit feedback type is specified.
---@field dataSplitEvalFraction? number The fraction of evaluation data over the whole input data. The rest of data will be used as training data. The format should be double. Accurate to two decimal places. Default value is 0.2.
---@field contributionMetric? string The contribution metric. Applies to contribution analysis models. Allowed formats supported are for summable and summable ratio contribution metrics. These include expressions such as `SUM(x)` or `SUM(x)/SUM(y)`, where x and y are column names from the base table.
---@field numFactors? string Num factors specified for matrix factorization models.
---@field includeDrift? boolean Include drift when fitting an ARIMA model.
---@field approxGlobalFeatureContrib? boolean Whether to use approximate feature contribution method in XGBoost model explanation for global explain.
---@field distanceType? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsDistanceTypeEnum|string Distance type for clustering models.
---@field l1RegActivation? number L1 regularization coefficient to activations.
---@field calculatePValues? boolean Whether or not p-value test should be computed for this model. Only available for linear and logistic regression models.
---@field timeSeriesDataColumn? string Column to be designated as time series data for ARIMA model.
---@field timeSeriesIdColumns? gcp.bigquery_v2.StringList The time series id columns that were used during ARIMA model training.
---@field tfVersion? string Based on the selected TF version, the corresponding docker image is used to train external models.
---@field fitIntercept? boolean Whether the model should include intercept during model training.
---@field trendSmoothingWindowSize? string Smoothing window size for the trend component. When a positive value is specified, a center moving average smoothing is applied on the history trend. When the smoothing window is out of the boundary at the beginning or the end of the trend, the first element or the last element is padded to fill the smoothing window before the average is applied.
---@field timeSeriesIdColumn? string The time series id column that was used during ARIMA model training.
---@field categoryEncodingMethod? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsCategoryEncodingMethodEnum|string Categorical feature encoding method.
---@field reservationAffinityValues? gcp.bigquery_v2.StringList Corresponds to the label values of a reservation resource used by Vertex AI. This must be the full resource name of the reservation or reservation block.
---@field treeMethod? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsTreeMethodEnum|string Tree construction algorithm for boosted tree models.
---@field labelClassWeights? gcp.bigquery_v2.DoubleMap Weights associated with each label class, for rebalancing the training data. Only applicable for classification models.
---@field hparamTuningObjectives? gcp.bigquery_v2.TrainingOptionsHparamTuningObjectivesItemEnumList The target evaluation metrics to optimize the hyperparameters for.
---@field subsample? number Subsample fraction of the training data to grow tree to prevent overfitting for boosted tree models.
---@field forecastLimitUpperBound? number The forecast limit upper bound that was used during ARIMA model training with limits.

